A||||7||Fast85GT||ECMs and PROMs||||5||
Z||000000||Fast85GT||08-02-2001||04:13 PM||||Where can I get a good scantool for my 85 GT? I don't want to pay $300.  I am trying to hook up my laptop.  Also, where can I get my PROM re-done for high performance?<P>------------------<BR>Jeremy H<BR>Black 1985 Pontiac Fiero GT||||reg||5
Z||000001||Leadfoot||08-02-2001||04:35 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fast85GT:<BR><B>Q:  Where can I get a good scantool for my 85 GT? I don't want to pay $300.<P>A:  If you want to read codes, you don't need one.  Just jumper pins A and B on the ALDL terminal (located right next to your cig lighter) and turn your ignition on.  Your service engine soon light will blink.  Count the number of blinks and look in the service manual to determine what code it is.  This procedure is explained in the haynes and chiltons manuals.<P>Q:  I am trying to hook up my laptop.  Also, where can I get my PROM re-done for high performance?<P>A:  The fierostore sells 2 types of performance PROMs.  Here is a website that tells you how to connect your laptop.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.euronet.nl/users/fo_elmo/techno.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.euronet.nl/users/fo_elmo/techno.htm</A> <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><p>[This message has been edited by Leadfoot (edited 08-02-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fast85GT||08-02-2001||05:16 PM||||I have been researching these sites, and making a cable is fine - I need the right software on my laptop.  What do I use for that?<P>------------------<BR>Jeremy H<BR>Black 1985 Pontiac Fiero GT||||reg||1
Z||000003||Terrybogin||08-02-2001||08:25 PM||||Don't buy an aftermarket chip. Buy the equipment and software to make your own. It is the only way to get "the right chip" for your particular combination.||||reg||1
Z||000004||terryk||08-03-2001||12:21 AM||||I agree with TerryB. You'll have to buy a burner and eraser, but with a scanner in hand you can tune the daylights out of it. <P>At the the same time, without some engine changes you won't gain much. <P>And contrary to what some people say, the GM ECM's are tons better than any of the aftermarket ECM/ECU.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Fast85GT||08-03-2001||01:24 PM||||OK! That is the info I'm looking for.  How do I do this? I need to erase the PROM and re-prog it.  I know.  How do I do that? Can I get a program for my laptop to do it?<BR><P>------------------<BR>Jeremy H<BR>Black 1985 Pontiac Fiero GT||||reg||1
Z||000006||Leadfoot||08-03-2001||04:42 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fast85GT:<BR><B>OK! That is the info I'm looking for.  How do I do this? I need to erase the PROM and re-prog it.  I know.  How do I do that? Can I get a program for my laptop to do it?<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Here is the website for the software. <A HREF="http://www.euronet.nl/users/fo_elmo/software.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.euronet.nl/users/fo_elmo/software.htm</A> <BR>I meant to see if it works but I have more pressing projects that I want to get done.  Good luck.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000007||rockcrawl||08-03-2001||06:23 PM||||I just took the leap and purchased all the equipment for burning PROMs. It's very cool stuff, I'm still getting acquainted with it. I bought a used Snap-On MT-2500 scanner from a local dealer. I've used a couple different types of scanners but after using the MT-2500, I don't think I'd want to use anything else, definitely worth the $200. I've been looking at all the PROMs I can get my hands on.||||reg||1
